{
  "id": "04394_suu",
  "headword": "{吸|す}う",
  "reading": "すう",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (godan)",
  "gloss": "to inhale, to suck",
  "conjugation": {
    "type": "godan",
    "ending": "う",
    "stem": "{吸|す}"
  },
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to inhale, to breathe in",
      "explanation": "To draw air or other gases into the lungs."
    },
    {
      "sense_number": 2,
      "gloss": "to smoke",
      "explanation": "To draw smoke from a cigarette into the mouth or lungs."
    },
    {
      "sense_number": 3,
      "gloss": "to suck, to sip",
      "explanation": "To draw liquid into the mouth, or for something to absorb liquid."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "04394_suu_ex1",
      "japanese": "{深|ふか}く{息|いき}を{吸|す}ってください。",
      "english": "Please take a deep breath.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "04394_suu_ex2",
      "japanese": "{タバコ}を{吸|す}いますか。",
      "english": "Do you smoke?",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        2
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "04394_suu_ex3",
      "japanese": "{蚊|か}に{血|ち}を{吸|す}われた。",
      "english": "A mosquito sucked my blood.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        3
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "04394_suu_ex4",
      "japanese": "{山|やま}の{新鮮|しんせん}な{空気|くうき}を{吸|す}った。",
      "english": "I breathed in the fresh mountain air.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "04394_suu_ex5",
      "japanese": "{鼻|はな}から{息|いき}を{吸|す}って、{口|くち}から{吐|は}いてください。",
      "english": "Breathe in through your nose and out through your mouth.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "04394_suu_ex6",
      "japanese": "ここは{禁煙|きんえん}なので{タバコ}は{吸|す}えません。",
      "english": "This is a non-smoking area, so you can't smoke here.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        2
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "04394_suu_ex7",
      "japanese": "{彼|かれ}は{一日|いちにち}に{一箱|ひとはこ}{タバコ}を{吸|す}う。",
      "english": "He smokes a pack of cigarettes a day.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        2
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "04394_suu_ex8",
      "japanese": "スポンジが{水|みず}を{吸|す}った。",
      "english": "The sponge absorbed the water.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        3
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "04394_suu_ex9",
      "japanese": "{赤|あか}ちゃんが{指|ゆび}を{吸|す}っている。",
      "english": "The baby is sucking its finger.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        3
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive). Intransitive pair: {吸|す}われる (passive). Pattern: Xを{吸|す}う (to inhale/suck X).\n\nASPECT: ている indicates habitual action. タバコを{吸|す}っている can mean 'smokes (habitually)' or 'is smoking.'\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {息|いき}を{吸|す}う (to inhale, breathe in)\n- {タバコ}を{吸|す}う (to smoke)\n- {空気|くうき}を{吸|す}う (to breathe air)\n- {血|ち}を{吸|す}う (to suck blood)\n\nCONTRAST:\n- {吸|す}う - to inhale/suck in\n- {吐|は}く - to exhale/spit out\n\nNOTE: {タバコ}を{吸|す}う is the standard expression for 'to smoke.'",
